# Build output
bin/
obj/
*.user
.vs/

# Installers â€” built artefacts (7 MB each). Only the CURRENT release is tracked, so a
# download is one click from the repo; older builds stay local. Update the exception
# when a new version ships, or the new installer will be silently ignored.
installer/Output/*
!installer/Output/Dawaii-Setup-2.8.exe

# Recovery scratch from the lost-drive incident â€” the recovered edits are all applied
_recovered/

# Local databases and their journals
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Test output
TestResults/

# Bot secrets. The committed appsettings.json carries an EMPTY token as a template; the real one
# comes from the ERP_TELEGRAM_TOKEN environment variable, or `dotnet user-secrets` for local work,
# both of which live outside the repository. These patterns catch the local override files someone
# will eventually paste a live token into. A leaked bot token can only be stopped by revoking it in
# BotFather — there is no way to un-publish it.
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.*.local.json
*.local.json

# Published bot output, which the installer packages. Self-contained, so a pharmacy PC needs no
# .NET 10 runtime and no internet to install one. DELETE THE FOLDER FIRST: `dotnet publish -o` never
# cleans, and anything left in there from a previous run is packaged into the installer and shipped.
#   rm -rf dist/bot
#   dotnet publish src/Erp.TelegramBot -c Release -r win-x64 --self-contained true -o dist/bot
dist/
